  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 256 AM MDT FRI AUG 28 2026\nTemperatures rebound closer to seasonal averages on Monday as\nshortwave ridging briefly takes hold. By Monday evening, the\nnext trough begins moving inland from the coast and may pull\nmonsoon moisture northward, supporting shower and thunderstorm\nchances primarily across south central Idaho. This trough will\nmove across the Pacific Northwest Tuesday into Wednesday\nbringing a threat for showers and thunderstorms across the\nhigher terrain. This feature will track ahead of a deeper low\npressure system set to move into the Pacific Northwest coast\nlate in the week. Consequently, expect enhanced cloud cover,\nintermittent shower and thunderstorm potential over higher\nterrain, and a tightening surface pressure gradient. Stronger,\nbreezy surface winds are likely heading into Thursday and Friday\nalong with another cooling trend. Ensemble spread remains\nslightly elevated regarding exact timing, but the overall signal\nfavors a cool, windy, and unsettled end to the extended period.",
